183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (Players may roam freely on their own side of the field besides anchors. Anchors tend to guard the centerzone against the dive. When a dive makes it to the centerzone but gets tackled, it is reset to the opposite team in the center of the quadrant closest to where the run started. A pass caught and tackled in the centerzone without reaching the ring does the same thing. The ball only has to cross the center ring lines for a point, a players feet do not have to be inside the ring.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (No player can cross the centerzone to go to the other half of the field with the exception of anchors. Players may enter the centerzone and return to their half. A player cannot score if they entered out of bounds either on purpose or on accident \(a shove or trip or tackle\) during the in-play run or throw.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
