endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (A player can save a ball from going out of bounds to the next team \(center of nearest quadrant that the ball went out of bounds at\), by using their feet to keep the ball elevated to put the ball back in play. A player can be standing out of bands and kick a ball through the air. If a player of the same team catches a saved kick in the center, then it is worth 5 points. If the opposing team catches the ball in the center, it is worth 5 points.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (If the ball is fumbled on a tackle, it is live until it goes out of bounds or a player recovers it. A recovered fumble resumes play with a stationary throw from the nearest quadrant that it was recovered in.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
